                      (    forth6809.asm):09398                                   ; MARKERW finished building its own header -
                      (    forth6809.asm):09399                                   ; wrong target. MARKER's own documented
                      (    forth6809.asm):09400                                   ; behavior is "forgets itself too" - traced
                      (    forth6809.asm):09401                                   ; MARKERW's own code and confirmed its
                      (    forth6809.asm):09402                                   ; snapshot (MKDP/MKCODE/MKVAR/MKLATEST) is
                      (    forth6809.asm):09403                                   ; taken at its very start, before HEADER or
                      (    forth6809.asm):09404                                   ; any compiling runs at all - so DOMARKER
                      (    forth6809.asm):09405                                   ; correctly restores to the state BEFORE the
                      (    forth6809.asm):09406                                   ; marker word itself was created (TSTCBUF
                      (    forth6809.asm):09407                                   ; directly), not the state right after. The
                      (    forth6809.asm):09408                                   ; real dictionary/compile mechanism was
