                      (    forth6809.asm):09507         ; Compiling-words test harness (glossary section 3.10). Reuses
                      (    forth6809.asm):09508         ; the scratch infrastructure established for sections 3.8/3.9
                      (    forth6809.asm):09509         ; (TSTCBUF/TSTCBUF2 for CODEHERE redirects, TSTFHDR for a fake
                      (    forth6809.asm):09510         ; dictionary header, TSTNAMEB for a fake source name). POSTPONE
                      (    forth6809.asm):09511         ; is this section's own hardest case: a genuine two-level
                      (    forth6809.asm):09512         ; compile-time mechanism (compiling code that, for a normal
                      (    forth6809.asm):09513         ; word, itself compiles a call to that word later, when the
                      (    forth6809.asm):09514         ; current definition eventually runs - not immediately, unlike
                      (    forth6809.asm):09515         ; every other compile-time word tested so far). ABORT" is safely
                      (    forth6809.asm):09516         ; testable for both its true and false flag cases - traced its
                      (    forth6809.asm):09517         ; own runtime behavior directly and confirmed it uses THROW -2
                      (    forth6809.asm):09518         ; internally, not the raw, never-returns ABORT mechanism plain
                      (    forth6809.asm):09519         ; ABORT itself uses (which remains untested, per section 3.1's
                      (    forth6809.asm):09520         ; own reasoning).
                      (    forth6809.asm):09521         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):09522         
                      (    forth6809.asm):09523         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):09524         ; TSTIMMED - unit test for IMMEDIATE. Builds a fake header (LEN/
