                      (    forth6809.asm):10183         ; TSTPOSTPONE1 - unit test for POSTPONE, normal (non-immediate)
                      (    forth6809.asm):10184         ; word case. Traced its own code first: for a normal word,
                      (    forth6809.asm):10185         ; POSTPONE compiles "[LIT xt][JSR COMPILE,]" into the current
                      (    forth6809.asm):10186         ; definition - NOT a direct call to the word itself. This is
                      (    forth6809.asm):10187         ; standard ANS semantics (POSTPONE appends a word's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):10188         ; compilation semantics to the current definition; for an
                      (    forth6809.asm):10189         ; ordinary word, that semantics IS "compile a call to it", so
                      (    forth6809.asm):10190         ; the current definition, when it later runs, must itself
                      (    forth6809.asm):10191         ; perform that compiling action against whatever definition is
                      (    forth6809.asm):10192         ; being compiled at that later point - not immediately). Given
                      (    forth6809.asm):10193         ; the genuine complexity of fully executing that second level
                      (    forth6809.asm):10194         ; (which would need a further redirected CODEHERE and a further
                      (    forth6809.asm):10195         ; round of execute-and-verify), this test instead verifies the
                      (    forth6809.asm):10196         ; compiled byte sequence directly - still a meaningful,
                      (    forth6809.asm):10197         ; unambiguous check of POSTPONE's own documented mechanism.
                      (    forth6809.asm):10198         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
C26F                  (    forth6809.asm):10199         TSTPOSTPONE1: LDD  CODEHERE
