                      (    forth6809.asm):12745         ; TSTDOTQUOTE - unit test for .". No STATE check at all in its
                      (    forth6809.asm):12746         ; own code (confirmed by reading it directly - matches "no
                      (    forth6809.asm):12747         ; interpretation semantics, per ANS" without a specific -14
                      (    forth6809.asm):12748         ; throw, unlike [CHAR]/S"), so only the compiling case is
                      (    forth6809.asm):12749         ; tested, matching how it's actually meant to be used. Its own
                      (    forth6809.asm):12750         ; runtime (DOTSTR) calls TYPE internally, which has two entirely
                      (    forth6809.asm):12751         ; different implementations gated by SERIALPOLL (the same real
                      (    forth6809.asm):12752         ; finding from section 3.1) - applying that lesson from the
                      (    forth6809.asm):12753         ; start here rather than re-discovering it: EMITCH works
                      (    forth6809.asm):12754         ; universally for a single-character check, but this outputs
                      (    forth6809.asm):12755         ; multiple characters, so - matching TSTCR's own established
                      (    forth6809.asm):12756         ; fix - the full OUTHEAD/OUTBUF check only applies under
                      (    forth6809.asm):12757         ; SERIALPOLL=0, with a narrower EMITCH-based check (last
                      (    forth6809.asm):12758         ; character only, plus the stack-depth check) for SERIALPOLL=1.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12759         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
