                      (    forth6809.asm):19778                                      ; Answers PADMINSIZE (84) directly, per
                      (    forth6809.asm):19779                                      ; ANS's own /PAD meaning (3.3.3.6, "the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19780                                      ; size of the scratch area whose address
                      (    forth6809.asm):19781                                      ; is returned by PAD") - PAD's own region,
                      (    forth6809.asm):19782                                      ; growing upward from PAD itself, distinct
                      (    forth6809.asm):19783                                      ; from HOLDMINSIZE above (which answers
                      (    forth6809.asm):19784                                      ; for a different region entirely, the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19785                                      ; downward-growing pictured-numeric buffer
                      (    forth6809.asm):19786                                      ; in the CODEHERE-to-PAD gap). PADOFFSET
                      (    forth6809.asm):19787                                      ; happens to equal PADMINSIZE numerically
                      (    forth6809.asm):19788                                      ; in this implementation (PADOFFSET EQU
                      (    forth6809.asm):19789                                      ; PADMINSIZE), but /PAD is answered with
                      (    forth6809.asm):19790                                      ; the conceptually correct constant, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):19791                                      ; the coincidentally-equal one.
FD85 FDD200070000     (    forth6809.asm):19792                  FDB   EN9,EN9L,0    ; NEW: FLOORED - previously the one item
                      (    forth6809.asm):19793                                      ; in this area explicitly left open
                      (    forth6809.asm):19794                                      ; pending its own investigation (unlike
                      (    forth6809.asm):19795                                      ; WORDLISTS, this is a CORE query, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):19796                                      ; tied to an unimplemented optional word
                      (    forth6809.asm):19797                                      ; set, so "false by omission" wasn't the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19798                                      ; right default). Investigated by tracing
                      (    forth6809.asm):19799                                      ; DIVCOMMON (shared by /, MOD, /MOD)
                      (    forth6809.asm):19800                                      ; against this system's own SM/REM and
                      (    forth6809.asm):19801                                      ; FM/MOD: DIVCOMMON restores the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19802                                      ; remainder's sign from DNSIGN (the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19803                                      ; dividend's own original sign) after
                      (    forth6809.asm):19804                                      ; dividing absolute values - exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):19805                                      ; SM/REM's own logic, confirmed identical
                      (    forth6809.asm):19806                                      ; by direct comparison. FM/MOD, by
                      (    forth6809.asm):19807                                      ; contrast, has an explicit flooring
                      (    forth6809.asm):19808                                      ; adjustment step (correcting the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19809                                      ; quotient and remainder when the
                      (    forth6809.asm):19810                                      ; quotient would be negative with a
                      (    forth6809.asm):19811                                      ; nonzero remainder) that DIVCOMMON does
                      (    forth6809.asm):19812                                      ; not have. This system's primary
                      (    forth6809.asm):19813                                      ; division words (/, MOD, /MOD) use
                      (    forth6809.asm):19814                                      ; symmetric division, not floored -
                      (    forth6809.asm):19815                                      ; FLOORED is 0 (false), a real, meaningful
                      (    forth6809.asm):19816                                      ; answer (recognized query, value false),
                      (    forth6809.asm):19817                                      ; not the "unrecognized" fallthrough
                      (    forth6809.asm):19818                                      ; WORDLISTS correctly uses.
